<section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap">
  <h1>Meet Our Tampa Bay Fishing Guides</h1>
  <p class="lead">Each of our captains fishes his own part of the bay in his own way. Tell us what you want to catch and who's coming, and we'll put you on the right boat.</p>
</div></section>
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="cap-row">
    <img src="/images/capt-ashmore.webp" alt="Capt. William Ashmore holding a redfish" width="640" height="411">
    <div>
      <h2>Capt. William "Dex" Ashmore</h2>
      <p class="tag">Florida native · 40+ years on the water · USCG 100 GRT Master</p>
      <p>Capt. Ashmore grew up in Florida and has fished Tampa Bay and Central Florida for more than 40 years. He holds a USCG Master license for vessels up to 100 gross tons. You may hear guests call him Dex.</p>
      <p>His guests talk about how he teaches. "We were novice fishermen and he instructed us quite well," wrote Eric M. Another guest, Jeff T., kept it shorter: "He can put you on the fish."</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="cap-row">
    <img src="/images/capt-pruner.webp" alt="Capt. David Pruner on the boat" width="1240" height="1023">
    <div>
      <h2>Capt. David Pruner</h2>
      <p class="tag">25 years fishing · Started on Indiana lakes</p>
      <p>Capt. Pruner's fishing started on the quiet lakes of Indiana with his dad, who taught him that patience and persistence are what catch fish. That lesson stuck through 25 years of fishing and a career on Tampa Bay.</p>
      <p>He still believes you never stop learning. He's happy to swap stories at the dock or try a technique he hasn't used before, and on a slow day he'll fish the bay the way it wants to be fished, taking whatever is willing to bite.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="cap-row">
    <img src="/images/capt-gonzales.webp" alt="Capt. Frankie Gonzales holding a snook" width="619" height="826" style="object-position:top">
    <div>
      <h2>Capt. Frankie Gonzales</h2>
      <p class="tag">30 years inshore · Tampa Bay and the southern Nature Coast</p>
      <p>Capt. Gonzales has fished the inshore water of west central Florida for 30 years, from Tampa Bay north into the southern Nature Coast. Guests trust him with their day on the water, and he takes that seriously.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="cap-row">
    <img src="/images/capt-hahn.webp" alt="Capt. Rob Hahn holding a gag grouper" width="1102" height="1400">
    <div>
      <h2>Capt. Rob Hahn</h2>
      <p class="tag">Master Diver · Decades offshore</p>
      <p>Capt. Hahn is a certified Master Diver. He has spent years underwater on the reefs, wrecks and ledges that most anglers only see on a sonar screen, and he has swum with the fish his guests are trying to catch.</p>
      <p>Above the water, he has decades of offshore fishing behind him. He knows when it's time to stay on a spot, move, or drop again.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
